# FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-20260923-121, author's second correction on the -67/-84
# blocker: the occurrence root is NOT external-only -- a method's own name resolves
# as a path root INSIDE its own body too. `probe\v` from within probe denotes the
# published occurrence cell of v, distinct from the bare local `v` (the activation
# cell): a direct write to the occurrence cell (bypassing the local's dirty-flag
# cache) and a read of it back, in the same activation, with no call boundary and
# no checkpoint between them. This is the minimal witness for that fact; the 7
# rewritten sticky/dirty fixtures (unit_arg_addr_*.lm2, unit_char_own_publish.lm2,
# unit_occ_sticky_selector.lm2) exercise the same mechanism under the sticky rule.
fn: probe () int
    size_t: v 3U
    size_t: g
    probe\v: 9U
    g: probe\v
    if: g != 9U
        return: 95
    if: v != 3U
        return: 96
    return: 0

return: probe()
